# <%= className %> web integration tests

Browser integration tests with [Playwright](https://playwright.dev). Headless by
default (`use.headless: true`), Chromium only out of the box.

## Setup

```bash
cd <%= fileName %>
npm install
npx playwright install chromium   # one-time browser download
cp .env.example .env              # or export BASE_URL
```

## Running

```bash
nx test <%= fileName %>           # headless
npm run test:headed               # watch it drive the browser
npm run test:ui                   # Playwright UI mode
npm run report                    # open the last HTML report
```

Point `BASE_URL` at the environment under test. Uncomment the `webServer` block
in `playwright.config.ts` to have Playwright start the app itself. Nx does not
cache this target.
